.TH SPINCLASS-BUILD-PINS 7 "" "spinclass" "Spinclass Reference"
.SH NAME
spinclass-build-pins \- build-time-pinned binaries (madder, direnv)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Spinclass exposes a Nix flake function
.B lib.mkSpinclass
that produces a spinclass binary with absolute
.I /nix/store
paths burned in for selected runtime tools.
At link time these paths are written into package-level Go variables
via
.B \-X
.IR ldflags ,
and the binary picks them up at runtime without consulting
.BR PATH .
.PP
The default
.B packages.default
output of the spinclass flake is
.B mkSpinclass {}
\(em no inputs supplied, all pinned paths empty, every integration
dormant.
A consumer flake that wants the integrations active calls
.B mkSpinclass
with the desired derivations:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
spinclass.lib.${system}.mkSpinclass {
  madder = madder.packages.${system}.default;
  direnv = pkgs.direnv;
}
.fi
.RE
.SH PINS
.SS madder
When the
.B madder
input is supplied,
.BR sc\ start " (and any other path that creates a worktree)"
initialises a per-worktree blob store at
.I <worktree>/.madder/local/share/blob_stores/default/
on first session creation.
The init command run is
.RS 4
.B madder init -encryption none .default
.RE
with
.B MADDER_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=<worktree>
set on the invocation only (not exported into the broader session) so
madder will not walk up into a parent repo's
.I .madder/
directory during store discovery.
.PP
The init step is guarded by an existence check on
.I blob_store-config
\(em rerunning
.B sc start
in a worktree that already has a store is a no-op.
.PP
When the integration is active, two additional rules are applied at
worktree creation:
.IP \(bu 2
.I .madder/
is appended to the worktree's
.IR .git/info/exclude .
.IP \(bu 2
.B Bash(madder:*)
is appended to the worktree's Claude Code allow list in
.IR .claude/settings.local.json .
.PP
When the
.B madder
input is null (the default
.BR packages.default ),
none of the above happens.
The feature is fully dormant; no
.I .madder/
directory is created and no madder-related allow rule is added.
.SS direnv
When the
.B direnv
input is supplied, spinclass invokes the pinned binary directly
instead of consulting
.BR PATH .
When the input is null, spinclass falls back to
.BR exec.LookPath ;
if no
.B direnv
is found, the
.I .envrc
generation step is skipped (this matches the pre-pin behaviour).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spinclass (1),
.BR spinclass\-sweatfile (5),
.BR madder (1),
.BR direnv (1)
